  "id": "be5c9230-0637-5f3e-851e-cd13c89de53e",
  "slug": "root-beer-float-poke-cake-recipe-11991819",
  "name": "Root Beer Float Poke Cake",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "This root beer float poke cake is moist, rich, and reminiscent of the classic soda shop treat. The distinctive flavor shines through in both the cake and the condensed milk soak for a nostalgic dessert packed with charm. Best of all, it starts with a boxed cake mix.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Coat a 13x9-inch baking pan with baking spray; set aside. Whisk together cake mix, eggs, oil, extract, if using, and 1 cup root beer in a large bowl. Spread batter evenly in the prepared pan."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a wooden pick inserted in center comes out clean, 28 to 32 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile, bring remaining 3 cups root beer to a boil in a saucepan over medium-high. Reduce heat to medium and simmer, stirring occasionally, until slightly thickened and reduced to 3/4 cup, about 30 minutes. Transfer 1/2 cup reduced root beer to a medium bowl; reserve the remaining 1/4 cup reduced root beer for serving. Whisk condensed milk into root beer in medium bowl."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "While the cake is still warm, using the round handle of a wooden spoon, poke holes all over top of cake, about 1 1/2 inches apart. Pour condensed milk mixture over cake, spreading evenly over top with a spatula. Cool to room temperature, about 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, beat cream and confectioner's sugar in a large bowl with an electric mixer on medium-high speed until stiff peaks form, 2 to 3 minutes. Spread evenly over cooled cake, and garnish with maraschino cherries. Serve with reserved reduced root beer. Recipe developed by Craig Ruff"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 60,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
